  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 multilayer stack on fused silica substrate for dual-band performance. Layer sequence: Air | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | Fused Silica. Initialize odd-layer positions (1,3,5,...,23) with random thickness between 20-40 nm. Initialize even-layer positions (2,4,6,...,24) with random thickness between 80-110 nm. Apply 5% periodic scaling perturbation to initial stack. Optimize all 24 layer thicknesses using gradient-based optimizer with evolutionary initialization. Evaluate performance at normal incidence, unpolarized light. Compute target score based on: maximize transmittance in 800-1500 nm band, maximize reflectance in 200-400 nm band. Total layer count fixed at 24. Materials: HfO2 (high index), SiO2 (low index). Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 6 alternating HfO2/SiO2 pairs (12 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 200-400 nm, 800-1500 nm. soft objectives: High transmission in 800-1500 nm band; High reflection in 200-400 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Low transmission in 200-400 nm band; Low reflection in 800-1500 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layers <= 30; Materials limited to HfO2 and SiO2.",
